hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1104","Narrated by Bundar, narrated by Abu Dawud, narrated by Abu Harra, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Saad bin Hisham Al-Ansari, that he asked Aisha about the Prophet’s prayer. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him at night. She said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “when he prayed the evening prayer, he would perform two rak’ahs, then he would sleep.” And before his head is his ablution and a toothbrush, so he gets up and uses his toothbrush, performs ablution, prays, and performs two rak’ahs, then he gets up and prays eight. He performed several rak'ahs in recitation, and he prayed Witr with the ninth, and he prayed two rak'ahs while sitting. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prescribed the Sunnah, Then he took the meat, made six of the eight, prayed Witr with the seventh, and prayed two rak’ahs while sitting, reciting in them: Say, O you disbelievers, and behold! \"it shook\""
"1105","Ali bin Sahl al-Ramli told us, Mummal bin Ismail told us, Amara bin Zazan told us, Thabit told us, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was “He performed the Witr prayer with nine rak’ahs, but when he became old and heavy, he performed the Witr prayer with seven rak’ahs, and prayed two rak’ahs while sitting, reciting: The Most Gracious, and \"The incident.\" Anas said: And we recite short surahs when they shake, and say, O disbelievers, and the like."
